            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Jillian"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Delicious! This is an oldie, but a goodie and it was a great way to use up some homemade waffles I made for breakfast. Instead of maple syrup I opted for hot fudge. Whatever combination of ice cream flavors or toppings this is sure to please!"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Allrecipes Member"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Growing up these were a very special treat at my dad's house - only we used 2 frozen waffles with ice cream sandwiched in between. Dad would buy the half gallon of ice cream in a rectangular cardboard box, let it sit on the counter to soften for a few moments and cut off ~1\" thick slices and place them in between 2 waffles. Great memories - thanks for posting this :)",
            "datePublished": "2011-03-16T18:35:27.600Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Sissy_Monroe"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I tried this with strawberry ice cream and some strawberry syrup instead of butter and maple syrup. The result is something like a waffle cone, delicious! It's a once in a while treat, but it's the perfect indulgence!",
            "datePublished": "2012-12-14T08:45:07.270Z"
          },
